["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/ContentIdentifierType/swhid", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "SoftWare Hash IDentifier, a persistent intrinsic identifier for digital artifacts, such as files, trees (also known as directories or folders), commits, and other objects typically found in version control systems. The format of the identifiers is defined in the [SWHID specification](https://www.swhid.org/swhid-specification/v1.2/) ([ISO/IEC 18670](https://www.iso.org/standard/89985.html)). They typically look like `swh:1:cnt:94a9ed024d3859793618152ea559a168bbcbb5e2`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/FileKindType", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Enumeration of the different kinds of SPDX file.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/requirementUUID", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The UUID used by a requirements management or any other lifecycle management tool to uniquely identify a requirement item. UUID, or universally unique ID, is a standard term in requirements engineering.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/test", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The Element is a test used to verify functionality on a software element.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
